.TH SDL_BindGPUFragmentStorageTextures 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_BindGPUFragmentStorageTextures \- Binds storage textures for use on the fragment shader.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_BindGPUFragmentStorageTextures(
.BI "    SDL_GPURenderPass *render_pass,
.BI "    Uint32 first_slot,
.BI "    SDL_GPUTexture *const *storage_textures,
.BI "    Uint32 num_bindings);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These textures must have been created with
.BR SDL_GPU_TEXTUREUSAGE_GRAPHICS_STORAGE_READ \[char46]
.PP
The textures being bound must have a matching type declared in the shader (2D, 3D, 2DMS, etc\[char46])
.PP
Be sure your shader is set up according to the requirements documented in
.BR SDL_CreateGPUShader ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I render_pass
a render pass handle\[char46]
.TP
.I first_slot
the fragment storage texture slot to begin binding from\[char46]
.TP
.I storage_textures
an array of storage textures\[char46]
.TP
.I num_bindings
the number of storage textures to bind from the array\[char46]
.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateGPUShader (3)
